WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:03.220
- Ooey-gooey and packed with
delicious, melty cheese.

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:06.000
Nothing says comfort like
a homemade mac and cheese.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.470
And today, we're gonna show you

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:10.119
how we make our favorite
baked mac and cheese.

00:00:10.119 --> 00:00:12.702
(upbeat music)

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:17.530
Countries across Europe were
creating versions of this dish

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:19.090
dating back to the Middle Ages.

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:22.240
There's even a recipe in a
14th century Italian cookbook

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:23.970
for sheet noodles cut into squares

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:25.500
and sprinkled with grated cheese.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.430
While serving as a diplomat in France,

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:29.570
Thomas Jefferson tried the French version

00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:31.400
and loved it so much, he requested

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:34.480
that his enslaved chef,
James Hemings, recreate it.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:37.060
Historians believe Hemings
should be given the true credit

00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:38.530
for bringing this dish to life.

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:40.870
Just like Hemings, many
other enslaved chefs

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:42.820
set the culinary example across America,

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:44.570
and often aren't credited for it.

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:47.840
Hemings' dish was served
in 1802 at a state dinner.

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:49.620
The dish grew in popularity from then on.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:51.490
So how do you make mac and cheese?

00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:54.240
There's only one place to
start and that's the noodles.

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:56.610
There's so many options
when it comes to pasta,

00:00:56.610 --> 00:01:00.760
there's radiatori,
fusilli, cavatelli, shells,

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:03.750
and probably most commonly
associated with mac and cheese,

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:04.583
elbows.

00:01:04.583 --> 00:01:06.980
We recommend any short, curly pasta.

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:09.870
We've decided that our favorite
pasta for mac and cheese

00:01:09.870 --> 00:01:10.870
are shells.

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:13.280
They're just the perfect size,
and their shape allows you

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:15.870
to get a beautiful burst
of sauce with each noodle.

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:17.070
So let's get cooking.

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:19.560
We're gonna boil the
pasta in well salted water

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:22.170
for two minutes less than
recommended on the package.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.000
You want the pasta to have a slight bite

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:26.150
because it'll actually
finish cooking in the oven.

00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:27.560
When it comes to mac and cheese,

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:29.440
there are two types of cheeses we need,

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:31.620
a melting cheese which adds to the texture

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:33.980
and a flavor cheese
which adds to the taste.

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:36.220
So what is an ideal melting cheese?

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:38.810
American and Velveeta are
both great melting cheeses

00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:40.810
because they have sodium citrate in them,

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:44.250
which as it melts gives
this creamy, gooey texture.

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:46.490
Mozzarella is also a good melting cheese

00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:49.590
because it's super creamy
and makes great cheese bowls.

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:52.640
But for our melting cheese
today, we're going with American.

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:54.190
And what makes a good flavor cheese?

00:01:54.190 --> 00:01:56.330
A few that are great for
flavor in your mac and cheese

00:01:56.330 --> 00:01:59.330
are fontina which has a
buttery and fruity flavor;

00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:02.220
Gruyere which has a sweet,
nutty, earthy flavor;

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:04.800
smoked Gouda which has a meat-like flavor;

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:07.330
Havarti which has a sweet, herby flavor;

00:02:07.330 --> 00:02:09.890
and cheddar which has a
bold and bright flavor.

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:12.550
We've chosen sharp cheddar
as our flavor cheese.

00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:14.210
This gives you the best of both worlds

00:02:14.210 --> 00:02:16.550
and creates the cheesiest, creamiest,

00:02:16.550 --> 00:02:18.390
and gooiest mac and cheese.

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:20.350
You always want to shred
the cheese yourself

00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:22.310
because the pre-shredded
cheese from the store

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:25.380
is usually coated in additives
that make it harder to melt.

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:27.020
Now, we all know mac and cheese

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:28.740
is only as good as its cheese sauce.

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:31.140
We're gonna start ours by
adding some butter to a pot.

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:32.230
Once it begins foaming,

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:34.020
we'll add some mustard powder and cayenne

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.660
and toast them for about a minute.

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:37.180
Seasoning the dish at this step

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:39.490
will really help to add depth of flavor.

00:02:39.490 --> 00:02:41.880
The spices will bloom and become aromatic

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:44.750
which will enhance their flavors
and boost their intensity.

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:46.460
Now while you can season
your mac and cheese

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:47.730
with anything you want,

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:50.080
we're keeping our recipe pretty simple.

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:51.670
The bit of heat from our spices

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:53.910
will help cut through the
richness of the cream sauce,

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:55.650
providing some nice balance.

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:57.050
Now to add our liquids.

00:02:57.050 --> 00:02:59.730
The three most common liquids
people use for mac and cheese

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:02.680
are usually milk, heavy
cream, and evaporated milk.

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:04.680
The biggest difference
between the three liquids

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:06.090
is their water content.

00:03:06.090 --> 00:03:08.410
We found the combination of
whole milk and heavy cream

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:11.040
gave the best flavor
and creamiest mouthfeel.

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:13.620
Once our liquids come to a
simmer, we'll add an egg.

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:16.270
This will give the mac and
cheese a custardy-like texture

00:03:16.270 --> 00:03:19.120
that helps the sauce bind
to the pasta really well.

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:20.560
Just be sure to temper your egg

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:23.210
by adding a little bit of
the warm milk mixture first.

00:03:23.210 --> 00:03:25.560
That way, we don't end
up with scrambled eggs.

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:26.990
Let's add our cheese.

00:03:26.990 --> 00:03:28.220
Now this is the tricky part

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:30.090
because while extremely satisfying,

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:31.890
things can go very wrong here.

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:33.980
Some cheeses melt differently than others,

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:36.410
causing the fat and oil
to begin to separate,

00:03:36.410 --> 00:03:38.410
resulting in a grainy sauce.

00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:41.370
But we've designed and our mac
and cheese to be foolproof.

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:42.780
Since we aren't using a roux,

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:44.770
our mac and cheese sauce won't crack.

00:03:44.770 --> 00:03:46.730
Another way to ensure
your sauce won't crack

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:48.390
is by adding cornstarch.

00:03:48.390 --> 00:03:50.270
Adding it directly to the cheese mixture,

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:51.550
rather than creating a slurry

00:03:51.550 --> 00:03:53.280
will help the sauce thicken more evenly

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:54.370
and prevent clumping.

00:03:54.370 --> 00:03:56.290
And the key to evenly melt the cheese

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:58.170
and ensure proper emulsification,

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:00.150
is to add the cheese off of the heat.

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:03.030
Keep stirring while adding
the cheese handful by handful.

00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:04.230
You'll know your sauce is done

00:04:04.230 --> 00:04:06.050
when the cheeses have melted smoothly

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:07.460
and it's slightly thickened.

00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:08.750
While the mac and cheese bakes,

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:10.650
the sauce will continue to thicken,

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:13.270
so we wanna make a super
creamy sauce to start

00:04:13.270 --> 00:04:14.920
so that when it's finished baking,

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:17.010
we don't end up with
the dry mac and cheese.

00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:19.570
We'll add our cooked shells
to our cheese sauce and coat.

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:21.640
Wow, I'm drooling.

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:25.530
Let's add this to the baking
dish and top with more cheese.

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:26.680
We found that the combination

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:29.410
of cheddar, mozzarella,
and Parmesan cheese,

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:30.740
creates the most delicious

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:33.330
and satisfyingly golden
brown and crispy top.

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:34.770
It's time to bake.

00:04:34.770 --> 00:04:37.150
We're focusing on the
classic baked version.

00:04:37.150 --> 00:04:38.160
Baking mac and cheese

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:40.440
allows you to get that crunchy, cheesy top

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:42.690
and the best corner pieces.

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:44.850
Some people cover their
Mac and cheese with foil

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:46.660
to help prevent the dish from drying out

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:47.620
while it's in the oven.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:49.470
We've made the ultimate saucy mac

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:51.530
and covered our entire dish in cheese,

00:04:51.530 --> 00:04:54.200
so we don't need to cover
it with anything additional.

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:57.230
Since we want crispy top to
compliment our saucy mac,

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:59.570
we wanna finish the
dish under the broiler.

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:01.630
The oven alone will help the topping melt,

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:03.410
but the broiler will give it that iconic

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:05.540
golden brown and crispy top we're after.

00:05:05.540 --> 00:05:07.940
It's the moment we've
all been waiting for.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:11.180
But hold on, before you
sacrifice the roof of your mouth

00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:13.230
for this ooey-gooey goodness,

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:14.840
make sure to let your mac and cheese rest

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:16.320
for at least five minutes.

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:18.180
This will allow the
sauce to set up a little

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:20.200
and achieve its maximum creaminess.

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:22.700
With mac and cheese, the
opportunities are endless.

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:27.220
You can have it as a side, in
a bread bowl, or simply as is.

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:29.570
It's filling, warm, and comforting.

00:05:29.570 --> 00:05:34.570
This mac and cheese is as
Gouda as it gets. Shell yeah.

00:05:34.753 --> 00:05:38.170
(upbeat music continues)

